# Description: On-demand todo_md task management rules and role/task workflow prompts
rule vitalio/todo_md:todo_md
[if role=design]
    [if task=]
        [if workspace=1] $ todo_md -w
        [if workspace!=1] $ todo_md
    [/if]
    [if task!=]
        [if piped!=1] $ todo_md {task:}
    [/if]
    prompt Mode: DESIGN. Explore requirements and architecture; once agreed, update AGENTS.md and .agents_bundle as needed, and record the design specification in TODO.md via todo_md (commit TODO*.md once backlog updates are finished); close the design task (D*) via todo_md done <ID> once architectural invariants are persisted in AGENTS.md (and docs/adr/) and follow-up implementation tasks are created.
[/if]
[if role=plan]
    [if task=]
        [if workspace=1] $ todo_md -w
        [if workspace!=1] $ todo_md
    [/if]
    [if task!=]
        [if piped!=1] $ todo_md {task:}
    [/if]
    prompt Mode: PLANNING. Decompose or compose (consolidate) work into self-contained tasks in TODO.md (default status NEW) depending on file, test, and documentation cohesion: refine or merge into an existing open task when the change touches the same files or tests, and split into separate tasks only when files, tests, and docs are independent; wire every new or refined task into open chains in both directions (upstream prerequisites via --depends on the new task, and downstream dependents via todo_md edit <ID> --depends ... on existing open tasks, doc/help alignment tasks, or orchestrator waves touching the same files or building on the new capability) so it is not left as an unintended standalone task; record target repository file paths and key symbol names (functions/classes) in backticks in each task body rather than brittle line ranges, promote ready prioritized tasks via todo_md next <ID>, and commit TODO*.md once backlog updates are finished; do not spawn a new session unless the user explicitly requests it.
[/if]
[if role=work]
    [if task=] var task=$(todo_md next-id --role work)
    [if task=]
        [if workspace=1] $ todo_md -w
        [if workspace!=1] $ todo_md
        prompt Mode: WORK. No [WIP] or [NEXT] task was resolved automatically; if the user supplied a task ID in the prompt, execute that task (starting with todo_md status <ID> WIP and a batched read of its target files in step 1), otherwise propose the top task shown in the todo_md overview above and ask for confirmation before editing.
    [/if]
    [if task!=]
        $ todo_md status {task:} WIP
        [if piped!=1] $ todo_md {task:}
        include $(todo_md files {task:} --max-lines 400 --max-total-lines 1200 --max-bytes 32768)
        prompt Mode: WORK (task={task:}). Emit your first run_block in this very first reply without restating the plan in chat: if all target files for task {task:} are already preloaded above, apply edits, run tests, and print the diff in step 1; otherwise run a single batched read step (using targeted grep/sed for large files) for any missing target files first. Deliver verified code, synced docs, and tests, run todo_md done {task:} inside the final commit step (after the diff is verified clean, immediately before staging and git commit, never during the edit step), record out-of-scope findings via todo_md add as problem/impact descriptions in default NEW status without --depends (staged into the same commit), and commit atomically.
    [/if]
[/if]
[if role=review]
    [if task=last] var task=$(todo_md last-id DONE)
    [if task=DONE] var task=$(todo_md last-id DONE)
    [if task=]
        [if workspace=1] $ todo_md -w
        [if workspace!=1] $ todo_md
        prompt Mode: REVIEW. Review the requested scope against active rules (checking TODO.md to avoid duplicates), report findings in chat, and after user agreement record remediation tasks in TODO.md via todo_md add and commit TODO*.md.
    [/if]
    [if task!=]
        [if piped!=1] $ todo_md {task:}
        include $(todo_md files {task:} --max-lines 400 --max-total-lines 1200 --max-bytes 32768)
        prompt Mode: REVIEW (task={task:}). Review task {task:} implementation, diff/commits, tests, and docs against the task specification and active rules (checking TODO.md to avoid duplicates), report findings in chat, and after user agreement record remediation tasks in TODO.md via todo_md add and commit TODO*.md.
    [/if]
[/if]
